WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
How this app is built. A code-generated walkthrough with a real synthetic decision run.
Silent video: read the on-screen captions. No personal data.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Less group chat. More actual plans.. Sign in with Google to start a real event, then enter a ZIP and activity ideas and share an invite. Everyone saves preferences before the group searches nearby venues.
This synthetic run saved 4 responses and chose Coffee and catch-up (demo). Members need no API keys. The demo needs no account.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Pick more than one good time. Members choose Can join, Maybe or Cannot join, pick activities, set a personal spending limit and share needs.
After members opt in, the coordinator can ask the LLM to explain a shared fit. Python checks shared choices; the coordinator still finalizes. Phone access requires secure hosting.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
A plan friends can afford. Each person saves a maximum spend. Known venue estimates must fit the event budget and every definite attendee limit.
Maybe stays tentative. Unknown cost needs checking; it is not a promise of affordability.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Suggestions need agreement. Python checks activity consensus, venue votes and budgets. The optional LLM explains only supplied choices and facts.
Every definite attendee must accept the venue. Only the coordinator confirms; AI never books or sends messages.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Real discovery, checked by humans. Simple ZIP tiles use Geoapify Places with a host-managed key. Unknown hours, ratings and prices need checking.
Neo4j and parallel advocates are legacy learning modules. This recording uses fictional places and no external API calls.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
From shared activity to a real plan. Venue tiles and ballots stay on the group page. 3 available or tentative demo members voted.
Their agreed fictional venue is Bluebird Corner (fictional). Real venue ratings and costs stay unknown until sourced.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
A meetup you can actually follow. 2026-10-24 at 6 PM Central, for 2 hours.
The group keeps its chosen venue and address together. Check hours and final costs before arranging a reservation. Fictional venues have no real route.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Reservations, texts and memories. Reservation made in this demo: no. Current meetup scrapbook entries saved: 1.
Upload photos in Our adventures: the group gallery refreshes automatically. Group settings supports leaving, coordinator transfer and optional deletion of your own memories.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Built to stay reviewable. The current source has 20 application modules and 104 test functions (not a test-pass count).
Help explains architecture and limitations. Run the watcher while coding; GitHub Actions rebuilds the artifact on pushes.
